{"study_accession":"PRJNA1440385","secondary_study_accession":"SRP685410","title":"Methylation of the Cg12712415 Locus Suppresses TAK1 Expression to Mediate Immune Paralysis in Severe Pneumonia","description":"Severe pneumonia lethality often arises not from excessive inflammation, but from subsequent immune system \"paralysis\" (immunoparalysis), a clinical challenge lacking specific biomarkers and effective therapies. Our study addressed this by identifying key epigenetic checkpoints driving immunoparalysis. Herein, we identify that DNA methylation at the Cg12712415 locus acts as an epigenetic switch to distinguish and predict secondary immunoparalysis in severe pneumonia patients. Mechanistically, DNMT3A specifically catalyzes this methylation, silencing transcription of the critical kinase TAK1 by blocking RNA polymerase II binding. TAK1 loss impairs monocyte/macrophage functions, disrupts intercellular crosstalk, induces CD8⁺ T cell exhaustion and regulatory T cell expansion, and causes systemic immunosuppression. Importantly, macrophage-derived exosome-mediated TAK1 delivery reversed immunoparalysis and improved survival in animal models. Our findings establish the \"DNMT3A–Cg12712415–TAK1\" axis as a novel regulatory pathway, provide a new immunoparalysis biomarker, and lay the foundation for an epigenetic-based targeted therapy. Overall design: RNA Extraction and Transcriptome Sequencing Total RNA was extracted from isolated and purified CD14⁺ monocytes using TRIzol reagent. Following ribosomal RNA (rRNA) depletion, sequencing libraries were constructed according to the Illumina library preparation protocol and subsequently sequenced on the Illumina Genome Analyzer II platform. ATAC‑seq A total of 1×10⁵ fresh cells were used for each assay. Libraries were constructed using Tn5 transposase treatment and sequenced on an Illumina platform. Raw reads were subjected to quality control using fastp and aligned to the reference genome with Bowtie2. PCR duplicates were removed using Picard, and MACS2 was used for peak calling to identify open chromatin regions (ATAC‑seq peaks). Identified peaks were annotated with HOMER, followed by transcription factor binding motif analysis. Chromatin Immunoprecipitation (ChIP) Log-phase cells were washed with PBS, cross-linked with 1% formaldehyde at room temperature for 10 min, and quenched with glycine. After lysis, chromatin was sonicated to 200–500 bp fragments. Chromatin was incubated with anti-RNA polymerase II antibody or control IgG pre-bound to Protein A/G magnetic beads at 4℃ overnight. After washing, elution, cross-link reversal and proteinase K digestion, DNA was purified and analyzed by qPCR for target region enrichment.","pubmed":"","geo_series":"","n_samples":18,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN56611036","study_accession":"PRJNA1440385","blood_class":"blood_cells","class_from":"sample","title":"Tolerant-LPS-C2","description":"Tolerant-LPS-C2","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM9605592","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2026-04-23","attributes":[["source_name","peripheral blood"],["tissue","peripheral blood"],["cell_type","monocytes"],["geo_loc_name","missing"],["collection_date","missing"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR37707215","experiment_accession":"SRX32584767","library_layout":"SINGLE","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina Genome Analyzer II","read_count":36692097,"base_count":3705901797,"first_public":"2026-04-23","experiment_title":"Illumina Genome Analyzer II sequencing: GSM9605592: Tolerant-LPS-C2 Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"}],"labels":[],"single_cell":false},{"sample_accession":"SAMN56611037","study_accession":"PRJNA1440385","blood_class":"blood_cells","class_from":"sample","title":"Tolerant-LPS-C1","description":"Tolerant-LPS-C1","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM9605591","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2026-04-23","attributes":[["source_name","peripheral blood"],["tissue","peripheral blood"],["cell_type","monocytes"],["geo_lo